      "richText": [
        [
          "What is the purpose of Spring Profiles?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80cb-ba8a-d4bb8ab5bc58",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "How do "
        ],
        [
          "@Value",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "@ConfigurationProperties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " differ?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-802c-b659-c81f117019c6",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "How do you define and activate different environments in Spring Boot?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80fd-ae24-c678760811a3",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "When would you use "
        ],
        [
          "@ConfigurationProperties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " over "
        ],
        [
          "@Value",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8097-a4ff-c7e9a0b652e9",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "How can you switch between profiles when running your app?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8069-8794-c25809b7ec7e",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f4-81a8-c4ad5ca68cc4",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "💡 5. Best Practices & Pitfalls"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d7-b786-c27d4438c53c",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "✅ Best Practices"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8026-91b7-c8af1096927e",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use "
        ],
        [
          "@ConfigurationProperties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " for grouped and reusable configs."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-806d-9d95-f68ebbaa0fda",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Clearly separate environment configs ("
        ],
        [
          "application-dev.properties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", etc.)."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f4-a4dd-e4b8c4cc4812",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Keep secrets (passwords, API keys) out of source control using external config servers or environment variables."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-802e-902e-c0b4510787cb",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "❌ Common Pitfalls"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-800c-a0fa-e8a28e1fbd57",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Forgetting to enable "
        ],
        [
          "@ConfigurationProperties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " by annotating the class or using "
        ],
        [
          "@EnableConfigurationProperties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8093-8499-f6853dac92be",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Hardcoding values instead of injecting them via configuration."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f4-916d-c1c26ed256ba",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Mixing profile-specific logic in the code instead of using separate config files."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80b2-9d16-d55ac77399d8",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d7-a460-cebfa059bc0c",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🔗 6. Connection to Other Concepts"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-807b-a9f0-d6de1b3b3dfb",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Closely tied to "
        ],
        [
          "Dependency Injection",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ": config values are injected into beans."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-806d-aee1-dc20ac2ce011",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Related to "
        ],
        [
          "Spring Boot Auto-Configuration",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", which often depends on properties."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-805c-be43-dd2726496efc",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Useful with "
        ],
        [
          "Spring Cloud Config",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " for centralized configuration management."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c0-b85a-d3c1152047f5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Helps with "
        ],
        [
          "Testing",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " by allowing specific profiles for test scenarios."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-800d-a47c-ede9ab52143e",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c7-900e-f6d593f45082",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🎤 7. Quick Interview Answers"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-800a-8d86-d8341268aadb",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Q: Can you explain what Spring Profiles and ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@ConfigurationProperties",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " are used for?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8079-989a-d16dbf5f6e80",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Sure! Spring Profiles let you load different configuration files depending on the environment—like dev, test, or prod—without changing code. @ConfigurationProperties allows you to map a group of related settings from your properties file into a single Java class. This keeps your configuration clean, organized, and easy to manage across environments."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-804a-8700-f52ac3408a65",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-profile-select",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Profile selection and typed settings"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-profile-select-b0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Activate dev with SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev or --spring.profiles.active=dev. Keep dev-only values in application-dev.yml and production values outside the source tree."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-profile-select-b1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Do not put spring.profiles.active inside a profile-specific document; profile activation belongs in a non-profile-specific source or a runtime override."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-profile-select-b2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use @Value for an isolated value. Use @ConfigurationProperties for related settings, especially when they need structured binding and validation."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-profile-select-b3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Binding a settings class is separate from registering it. Use @ConfigurationPropertiesScan or @EnableConfigurationProperties for the class."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ed-profile-select-b4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Profile changes happen at application startup. Changing an environment variable does not automatically rebuild existing bean instances."
        ]
      ]
    }
